# vLLM nightly af7f9488, TP2 + EP2 over one 400G RoCE link, Humming 3-bit WNA16 MoE backend, 408 GiB/rank of routed
# experts (routed_experts.{w13,w2}_weight_packed) in Grace memory via UVA, load hook recipes/kimi-k3/vllm/hook.
# Run 2026-10-09 08:30-09:37 PT (attempt 2 of this session; attempt 1 is the OOM shown at the end). Rank 1 (right) first.
# Excerpt: lines selected verbatim from the raw files named below; hostnames, IPs, user names and GPU UUIDs replaced
# with <placeholders>. vllm bench "Namespace(...)" argument dumps are cut to the fields that define the run (marked).
# "power-summary" lines are computed by us from the 1 s nvidia-smi samples of the named csv (GB300 rows only).
# Times are Pacific (PT) unless the line says otherwise; vLLM server log lines are UTC ("10-09 15:31:05" = 08:31:05 PDT).
# Bench harness: an older version of the bench script (random 8,192 in / 1,024 out, ignore-eos, decode_agg = C x 1000 /
# mean TPOT). It used seed 1006+rep for EVERY concurrency, so C4 and C16 reused C1 rep 1's seed 1007, and prefix caching
# was ON in the server. C1 (three fresh seeds) and C4 show a 0.0% prefix-cache hit rate; the C16 run does not (see the
# "prefix cache" section): treat C16 as an upper bound.


